{"content_hash": "111c7a2427f9423e", "version_id": 163, "article_id": 17, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "How Nature Index tables are made for infectious diseases", "title_zh": "《自然指数》传染病表格是怎么做出来的", "topic": "science", "source": "nature", "source_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02999-z", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52462408254_7688613222_b.jpg", "credit": "DCHNwam · pdm 1.0 · via flickr"}, "published_date": "2026-10-07", "word_count": 183, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "Nature Index has published a guide to its tables for the 2026 Spotlight on Infectious Diseases. The tables rank research using a special database, and the guide explains the method behind them.", "lead_zh": "《自然指数》发布了一份指南，介绍2026年传染病专题的表格是如何制作的。这些表格使用一个特殊数据库对研究进行排名，指南解释了背后的方法。", "preview": "The tables for the 2026 Nature Spotlight on Infectious Diseases come from the Nature Index database. They cover articles about infectious di", "preview_zh": "2026年《自然》传染病专题的表格来自《自然指数》数据库。它们涵盖2021年至2025年间发表的传染病文章。这些文章发表在自然科学和健康科学期刊上，因此数据聚焦于这些领域的近期研究。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 153, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@d7bba21/content/audio/17/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 76.925, "size_bytes": 465408, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 200, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@d7bba21/content/data/versions/163.json", "paragraphs": ["The tables for the 2026 Nature Spotlight on Infectious Diseases come from the Nature Index database. They cover articles about infectious diseases that were published between 2021 and 2025. These articles appeared in natural-science and health-science journals, so the data focus on recent research in these fields.", "To find the articles, the team searched titles and abstracts in Digital Science's Dimensions database. They looked for 83 infectious diseases and also included five subcategories for severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes. The search strings were the same as those used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious Disease report.", "After the search, the team kept only the articles that were also in the Nature Index database. These articles formed the final data set for the tables in this Spotlight. Although the method is simple, it helps readers understand how the rankings are built and what they include.", "The guide also notes that the Spotlight is editorially independent. Advertisers have no influence over the content, so the tables and articles remain separate from commercial interests. This is important because readers need to trust the information they see."], "paragraphs_zh": ["2026年《自然》传染病专题的表格来自《自然指数》数据库。它们涵盖2021年至2025年间发表的传染病文章。这些文章发表在自然科学和健康科学期刊上，因此数据聚焦于这些领域的近期研究。", "为了找到这些文章，团队在Digital Science的Dimensions数据库中搜索了标题和摘要。他们查找了83种传染病，还包括5个严重冠状病毒和流感亚型的子类别。搜索字符串与2021年《自然指数》传染病报告使用的相同。", "搜索后，团队只保留了同时也在《自然指数》数据库中的文章。这些文章构成了本次专题表格的最终数据集。尽管方法简单，但它帮助读者理解排名是如何建立的以及包含哪些内容。", "指南还指出，该专题在编辑上是独立的。广告商对内容没有影响，因此表格和文章与商业利益保持分离。这一点很重要，因为读者需要信任他们看到的信息。"], "body": "The tables for the 2026 Nature Spotlight on Infectious Diseases come from the Nature Index database. They cover articles about infectious diseases that were published between 2021 and 2025. These articles appeared in natural-science and health-science journals, so the data focus on recent research in these fields.\n\nTo find the articles, the team searched titles and abstracts in Digital Science's Dimensions database. They looked for 83 infectious diseases and also included five subcategories for severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes. The search strings were the same as those used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious Disease report.\n\nAfter the search, the team kept only the articles that were also in the Nature Index database. These articles formed the final data set for the tables in this Spotlight. Although the method is simple, it helps readers understand how the rankings are built and what they include.\n\nThe guide also notes that the Spotlight is editorially independent. Advertisers have no influence over the content, so the tables and articles remain separate from commercial interests. This is important because readers need to trust the information they see.", "body_zh": "2026年《自然》传染病专题的表格来自《自然指数》数据库。它们涵盖2021年至2025年间发表的传染病文章。这些文章发表在自然科学和健康科学期刊上，因此数据聚焦于这些领域的近期研究。\n\n为了找到这些文章，团队在Digital Science的Dimensions数据库中搜索了标题和摘要。他们查找了83种传染病，还包括5个严重冠状病毒和流感亚型的子类别。搜索字符串与2021年《自然指数》传染病报告使用的相同。\n\n搜索后，团队只保留了同时也在《自然指数》数据库中的文章。这些文章构成了本次专题表格的最终数据集。尽管方法简单，但它帮助读者理解排名是如何建立的以及包含哪些内容。\n\n指南还指出，该专题在编辑上是独立的。广告商对内容没有影响，因此表格和文章与商业利益保持分离。这一点很重要，因为读者需要信任他们看到的信息。", "text": "The tables for the 2026 Nature Spotlight on Infectious Diseases come from the Nature Index database. They cover articles about infectious diseases that were published between 2021 and 2025. These articles appeared in natural-science and health-science journals, so the data focus on recent research in these fields. To find the articles, the team searched titles and abstracts in Digital Science's Dimensions database. They looked for 83 infectious diseases and also included five subcategories for severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes. The search strings were the same as those used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious Disease report. After the search, the team kept only the articles that were also in the Nature Index database. These articles formed the final data set for the tables in this Spotlight. Although the method is simple, it helps readers understand how the rankings are built and what they include. The guide also notes that the Spotlight is editorially independent. Advertisers have no influence over the content, so the tables and articles remain separate from commercial interests. This is important because readers need to trust the information they see.", "vocab": [{"word": "infectious disease", "pos": "noun", "zh": "传染病", "note": "由病原体引起并能在人与人之间传播的疾病"}, {"word": "database", "pos": "noun", "zh": "数据库", "note": "有组织地存储数据的系统，便于搜索和检索"}, {"word": "abstract", "pos": "noun", "zh": "摘要", "note": "学术论文开头的简短总结"}, {"word": "journal", "pos": "noun", "zh": "期刊", "note": "定期出版的学术杂志"}, {"word": "subcategory", "pos": "noun", "zh": "子类别", "note": "大类之下更细的分类"}, {"word": "methodology", "pos": "noun", "zh": "方法论", "note": "研究或工作所使用的方法体系"}, {"word": "ranking", "pos": "noun", "zh": "排名", "note": "根据某种标准排列的顺序"}, {"word": "editorially independent", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "编辑独立的", "note": "内容不受广告商或赞助方影响"}, {"word": "advertiser", "pos": "noun", "zh": "广告商", "note": "付费投放广告的公司或个人"}, {"word": "influence", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "影响", "note": "对某事产生作用或改变"}], "title_original": "A guide to Nature Index tables", "summary_original": "Nature, Published online: 07 October 2026;\ndoi:10.1038/d41586-026-02999-z\nInformation on the methodology used in the ranking for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases.", "body_original": "SPOTLIGHT\n07 October 2026\nA guide to Nature Index tables\nInformation on the methodology used in the ranking for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases.\nEmail\nBluesky\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nReddit\nWhatsapp\nX\nSave article\nView saved research\nThe tables for the 2026\nNature Spotlight: Infectious diseases\nare based on the\nNature Index database\nand cover infectious-disease articles published in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025.\nNature Spotlight: Infectious diseases\nA keyword search on abstracts and titles was conducted to extract infectious-disease articles in Digital Science’s Dimensions database (Digital Science is part of Holtzbrinck, the majority shareholder of\nNature\n’s publisher, Springer Nature). The search covered 83 infectious diseases and included 5 subcategories to cover severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes. The\ndiseases and their Dimensions search strings\nwere the same as those for\nNature Index 2021 Infectious disease\n. The Dimensions articles identified that 